<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Fast DDS profile for robots that publish full Ouster point clouds.

  THE PROBLEM THIS SOLVES. rmw_fastrtps creates its shared-memory segment at a
  512 KiB default (measured: every /dev/shm/fastrtps_* file was 549408 bytes on
  both Bunkers). An OS-0-64 at 512x10 with point_type "original" is 48 B/point
  x 64 x 512 = 1.57 MB per PointCloud2, three times one segment. The result,
  measured 2026-09-01 on aslan_0 and botman_0: /ouster/points delivered at
  2.3 to 4.8 Hz against a configured 10 Hz, with stalls up to 2.3 s, and
  /laser_odometry starved with it (1.87 Hz on Aslan).

  It is specifically a delivery problem, not a production or CPU problem. The
  same os_driver node publishes /ouster/scan at 9.999 Hz (2.5 ms std dev) and
  /ouster/imu at 100 Hz off the same LidarScan, while using 8.9% of one core.
  Both robots were under 40% load. Botman has net.core.rmem_max=8388608 and
  Aslan has 212992, and they starved identically, so it is not the socket
  buffer either.

  16 MB gives ten clouds of headroom, which covers KeepLast(2) on a reliable
  reader plus in-flight fragments. tmpfs pages are allocated on write, so the
  segment costs what is actually used, not 16 MB per participant.

  useBuiltinTransports must be false. Leaving it true ADDS the builtin
  transports, which would put a second 512 KiB SHM transport alongside this one.
  UDPv4 is listed explicitly because dropping it would cut off every participant
  that does not share this host's /dev/shm.

  Applied via FASTRTPS_DEFAULT_PROFILES_FILE on the containers that carry the
  cloud: lidar (the writer), slam and nav2 (the two readers). Verify it took
  effect by the segment size, not by the log:
      ls -la /dev/shm/ | grep fastrtps | awk '{print $5}' | sort -n | uniq -c
  A size of 549408 means this file was NOT loaded.
-->
<dds xmlns="http://www.eprosima.com/XMLSchemas/fastRTPS_Profiles">
  <profiles>
    <transport_descriptors>
      <transport_descriptor>
        <transport_id>swarmdeck_shm</transport_id>
        <type>SHM</type>
        <segment_size>16777216</segment_size>
        <maxMessageSize>16777216</maxMessageSize>
      </transport_descriptor>
      <transport_descriptor>
        <transport_id>swarmdeck_udp</transport_id>
        <type>UDPv4</type>
      </transport_descriptor>
    </transport_descriptors>

    <participant profile_name="swarmdeck_large_data" is_default_profile="true">
      <rtps>
        <userTransports>
          <transport_id>swarmdeck_shm</transport_id>
          <transport_id>swarmdeck_udp</transport_id>
        </userTransports>
        <useBuiltinTransports>false</useBuiltinTransports>
      </rtps>
    </participant>
  </profiles>
</dds>
